Primitive implementation functions:

GetClass(ObjectPointer) 
  returns  the  pointer to the class description of the argument
object.

GetField(ObjectPointer,FieldOffset) 
  returns  the  contents  of  the  field indexed by FieldOffset.
This reference may be an integer or a pointerto an object.  Note
that the field begins with index 1.

StoreField(ObjectPointer,FieldOffset,Value) 
  returns  the  argument  ObjectPointer  after  storing the give
Value  in  the  field indexed lby FieldOffset.  The field offset
must  range  from  1  to  the  number of fields created for that
object.

Execute(ObjectPointer) 
  returns  results  of from the execution of the code pointed to
by  ObjectPointer.  A check is made to insure that the object to
be executed is of type CODE.

NewInstance(ClassObjectPointer NumberOfFields)

  creates   a   new   object   with  its  class  pointer  set to
ClassObjectPointer and NumberOfFields allocated for it.  Returns
the pointer to the new object. 
